 n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229892,"global_rank":112675},{"name":"waltmck/ipl-laser","owner":"waltmck","html_url":"https://github.com/waltmck/ipl-laser","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229887,"global_rank":112690},{"name":"mpnunez/SplendorBot","owner":"mpnunez","html_url":"https://github.com/mpnunez/SplendorBot","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Bot for playing Splendor","topics":[],"score":229887,"global_rank":112693},{"name":"hbergen/dbt-core-quickstart","owner":"hbergen","html_url":"https://github.com/hbergen/dbt-core-quickstart","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"dbt tutorial with jaffle-shop-template database","topics":[],"score":229887,"global_rank":112694},{"name":"davidmckennirey/arves","owner":"davidmckennirey","html_url":"https://github.com/davidmckennirey/arves","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":10,"language":"Python","description":"Automated Recon, Enumeration, and Vulnerability Scanner","topics":[],"score":229880,"global_rank":112715},{"name":"saugatt/traceroute-project","owner":"saugatt","html_url":"https://github.com/saugatt/traceroute-project","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229863,"global_rank":112734},{"name":"brady800526/Practice-Blockchain-Snakecoin_Python","owner":"brady800526","html_url":"https://github.com/brady800526/Practice-Blockchain-Snakecoin_Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"sc